def main():
 protect();pair=read(R/'10_mesh_hierarchy/PAIR_PRE_SOLVER_QUALIFICATION.json');assert pair['passed'];o=read(R/'ORIGINAL_FAILURE_METRICS.json');a=read(R/'06_recovered_M1/M1_C1/PRE_SOLVER_QUALIFICATION.json');b=read(R/'07_refined_M2/M2_C1/PRE_SOLVER_QUALIFICATION.json');f1=read(R/'06_recovered_M1/M1_C1/SOURCE_FIDELITY.json');f2=read(R/'07_refined_M2/M2_C1/SOURCE_FIDELITY.json');local=rows(R/'LOCAL_NODE_DISPLACEMENTS.csv');decision=read(R/'14_reproducibility/FINAL_DECISIONS.json');trial=read(R/'14_reproducibility/LOCAL_TRIAL_LEDGER.json')[0]
 docs={
 'HISTORICAL_FAILURE_REPRODUCTION.md':('Historical failure reproduced','The original C02 M1 candidate was copied and independently reconstructed without overwriting E10. Its 145,527 nodes and 82,498 Tet10 elements reproduce minimum SICN -0.1083067367 and minimum sampled determinant -0.0139227176 mm³. Exactly two elements fail. Gmsh element tags are 38861 and 45699; array indices are 4560 and 11398. A hypothetical index-based native export would number them 4561 and 11399; no native model was submitted.\n\nThe complete original mesh was rechecked, including SICN P01/P05/P50, every 73-point determinant set, corner orientation and the shared-edge map. Independent scalar checks reproduce the failures. Evidence: ORIGINAL_FAILURE_METRICS.json and 00_integrity/baseline.'),
 'SOURCE_AND_CAD_INTEGRITY.md':('Source and CAD preserved','All 336 durable E10 artifacts and 158 initially frozen E9 files were hash-verified at initialization. Original C02 source XYZ, IDs, T0 triangles, area weights and normals were copied byte-for-byte. No other source was analysed. The qualified STEP SHA256 remains 811aa69622f56d6dcfac1c483b3309fc3ad974b6a82e46762770c5d488e7b80a. No CAD geometry was regenerated.\n\nThe identity source-to-computational transform and inherited numerical X/Y axes are explicit. Physical axis calibration was not newly validated. All historical roots remain read-only. Final preservation checks and the release manifest cover the exact bytes.'),
 'INVALID_TET10_ROOT_CAUSE.md':('Verified numerical root cause','The two invalid elements share an internal face and belong to one topological region. Their corner determinants are +0.1112030880 and +0.1050155577 mm³; corner volumes are 0.0185338480 and 0.0175025929 mm³. Minimum face angles are about31.60 degrees and edge ratios are below1.79. The corners are not inverted or degenerate.\n\nThe shared measured-front midside, Gmsh node15562, is on the frozen CAD and lies0.078674563 mm below the corresponding straight-edge midpoint. In an independent diagnostic, straightening only that midside makes both local maps positive: Q2 minima0.0987557545 and0.0730502132 mm³. This off-CAD diagnostic is not an admissible repair and was not saved as a full candidate. It isolates the numerical contribution of boundary curvature.\n\nThe supported mechanism is curved boundary placement incompatible with the original straight interior quadratic layout. Gmsh ordering, the intended SOLID187 permutation and globally shared midsides are correct. The failure is not evidence of a measured-source defect or a rear/cap junction problem. S1 subsequently restored validity by moving one eligible interior midside only. See ROOT_CAUSE_HYPOTHESIS_MATRIX.csv and SINGLE_MIDSIDE_CAUSAL_DIAGNOSTICS.csv.'),
 'INVALID_ELEMENT_LOCAL_TOPOLOGY.md':('Local topology and support','Face-based one-ring and two-ring regions contain6 and15 elements respectively, including the two invalid elements. Both failures share one internal face. The four selected free midsides influence14 elements through their complete node-support stars, which are more inclusive than face-ring adjacency. All14 are verified after repair; no shared node is moved independently in different elements.\n\nLocal measured source IDs, XYZ and T0 weights are listed in ORIGINAL_SOURCE_POINTS_IN_LOCAL_WINDOW.csv. Boundary/interior classifications, patch distances and the unchanged geometry-only height0.5mm contour are retained. This contour is not a validated physical weld-toe track. Rear and cap interfaces are distant from the failure region.'),
 'QUADRATIC_NODE_ORDERING_AUDIT.md':('Tet10 ordering audit','Gmsh type11 local coordinates were obtained from the installed API. Midpoints were matched to their corner-edge pairs. Conversion to the native-style edge order is the zero-based permutation [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9,8]. Existing C02 E8B native-displacement provenance confirms this historical export convention without invoking ANSYS.\n\nThe whole original M1 edge map has122,410 unique edges and zero inconsistent shared midsides. No corner is reused as a midside. New M1 retains the original connectivity exactly; M2 independently passes the same conformity checks. See NODE_ORDERING.json and INVALID_ELEMENT_CONNECTIVITY.csv.'),
 'CORNER_VS_MIDSIDE_FAILURE.md':('Corner versus quadratic failure','Both original straight corner tetrahedra have positive determinants and ordinary local aspect measures. The full ten-node mapping is nevertheless inverted at sampled corners once the measured-front curvature is represented. Individual-midside diagnostics distinguish the shared boundary midside from the remaining positions.\n\nThe accepted repair preserves that CAD-constrained midside. Instead, one of the four eligible interior midsides moves; the other three stay exactly fixed. This changes the volume interpolation while keeping all corners and the entire external quadratic surface exactly fixed. No smoothing or coordinate change is applied to the measured surface.'),
 'LOCAL_REPAIR_PROTOCOL.md':('Frozen local repair protocol','Strategy precedence is S1, then S2, then S3 if needed. S1 minimizes the sum of squared node displacements normalized by the local length0.663101976 mm. Only four interior midsides are variables; all corners, boundary nodes and connectivity are fixed. Shared nodes have one global position.\n\nThe first trial used a0.035 quality-margin target, a per-node displacement cap0.15 times the local length, constrained SLSQP and120 maximum iterations. Constraints cover909 frozen Q2 positions in all14 potential-support elements. Frozen acceptance remains SICN≥0.020 and strictly positive determinants; the tighter optimizer target is not a relaxed gate. Whole-mesh quality, independent SICN, scalar derivatives, topology and fresh full-source geometry checks follow optimization.\n\nMaximum budgets remain3 strategies,3 trials per strategy,2 new full M1 candidates and2 new full M2 candidates. No native or AI execution is allowed. The exact preregistration and Q2 hash precede the local experiment.'),
 'LOCAL_REPAIR_EXPERIMENTS.md':('Bounded repair experiment','One S1 local trial was executed. It terminated after6 optimizer iterations, with objective0.000878214819 and maximum displacement0.0196508211 mm. Four interior midsides were eligible variables, but only Gmsh node86669 actually moved. Nodes86668,86670 and100559 remained byte-identical. Exact old/new coordinates and the full-coordinate audit are retained.\n\nOptimizer success was not used as acceptance. One complete M1 candidate was saved and passed full independent qualification. S2 and S3 were not executed because the least invasive strategy succeeded. Twelve one-midside counterfactual calculations are root-cause diagnostics on individual elements, not repair trials or full mesh candidates. No random perturbation or global M1 remeshing occurred.'),
 'REPAIRED_M1_FIDELITY.md':('M1 geometry fidelity','All original source arrays and the STEP are unchanged. Every external M1 mesh node, every corner and all connectivity entries are exactly identical to the original M1. Fresh full-source forward P95/max are0.001928801/0.008699451 mm. Reverse values are0.002744363/0.023077044 mm. All frozen0.010/0.040 mm gates pass.\n\nThese values match the original surface because S1 changes only interior interpolation. Actual curved-patch closest diagnostics and full patch classification were also evaluated. Local closest searches are not certified global closest distances and never substitute for the same-XY gates. Source IDs and weights remain bitwise preserved.'),
 'REPAIRED_M1_QUADRATIC_QUALITY.md':('Recovered M1 quality','M1_C1 retains145,527 nodes and82,498 Tet10 elements. Minimum SICN is0.0349999999912; minimum Q1 determinant is0.00444250194702 mm³. Negative, zero and below0.020 SICN counts are all zero. All73 original points were checked for every element. Independent SICN agrees with Gmsh across the complete mesh to3.963e-13.\n\nQ2 uses909 points on each of14 potential-support elements. Exact rational cubic Bernstein coefficients are positive for all14, with lower bound0.00444250194703 mm³. This is a continuous determinant positivity certificate for those stored local elements only. It is not a whole-mesh mathematical certificate. Node and element limits, shared identities, one connected volume, closed Euler-2 boundary and all measured/assumed patches pass.'),
 'M2_GENERATION_AND_REFINEMENT.md':('M2 generation after M1 qualification','M2 was generated only after the complete M1 pass receipt. Uniform eight-child subdivision of all M1 elements would exceed the230,000-element cap, so a permitted independently generated M2 was selected. The unchanged STEP was used. Near-weld size is0.30 mm, parent size0.60 mm, bulk maximum2.50 mm and growth1.0.\n\nA deterministic front-only local size constraint refines the original failure region: centerXY(128.753239,31.783374) mm, radius1.2 mm, minimum0.30 mm with smooth transition to parent size. This geometric choice was frozen before M2 generation and uses no stresses. One M2 candidate was generated in34.3309494 s. No M2 repair or additional improving candidate was needed.'),
 'M2_GEOMETRY_FIDELITY.md':('M2 geometry fidelity','M2 source forward P95/max are0.001842450/0.007785679 mm; reverse P95/max are0.002700924/0.024530793 mm. The same frozen measured coordinates and original T0 triangles define the reference. All geometry gates pass, and all six measured/assumed patches are classified.\n\nM2 is a different finite quadratic approximation of the same authoritative CAD. The symmetric actual quadratic chart comparison against M1 has maximum0.011574564 mm; bounded local-patch closest diagnostic maximum is0.011532917 mm. These are actual curved-face comparisons, not corner-facet distances. Same-CAD identity and per-source fidelity gates establish domain compatibility; no unstated pair-distance tolerance was introduced.'),
 'M2_QUADRATIC_QUALITY.md':('M2 quadratic quality','M2_C1 has193,962 nodes and109,737 Tet10 elements. Minimum SICN is0.0634291190 and minimum whole-mesh Q1 determinant is0.00450120191734 mm³. No negative/zero Q1 determinant or below0.020 SICN element was found. Global independent SICN agrees with Gmsh to5.575e-13.\n\nExpanded909-point checks pass on51 selected elements around the original failure region and lowest-quality elements. Exact rational Bernstein bounds are positive on the16 lowest-SICN elements. Continuous positivity of all other elements is not claimed. Parameter-coordinate metadata warnings from Gmsh are preserved; the labelled discrete MSH round trip verifies exact nodes, connectivity, physical patch names and recomputed SICN. These warnings are not native ANSYS shape checks.'),
 'M1_M2_HIERARCHY.md':('Achieved mesh hierarchy','Near-weld M1 median/P90 edges are0.400617341/0.412006779 mm. M2 achieves0.300664474/0.305606160 mm. Ratios are0.750502893 and0.741750319, both below the frozen0.98 ceiling. Curved-front face density increases by1.764946831.\n\nNear-weld face counts are14,077 and24,853; curved areas are963.186977 and963.491049 mm². Overall element-density ratio is1.330177701. Parent-region edge statistics are retained separately. Both meshes have the same CAD hash and source provenance. Quadratic volume quadrature gives33,562.48701696 and33,562.49316480 mm³, a difference0.00614784 mm³. This is discretization comparison, not measured volume validation.'),
 'MECHANICAL_MESH_PREFLIGHT.md':('Mechanical mesh geometry preflight','Both meshes preserve global-X tension, global-Y weld direction, full28 mm Y span, documented nominal19 mm thickness and the frozen parent-midpoint line atY30 andZ-9.37643484024406 mm. Defined reference force is53,200 N. Port surfaces are identifiable, their quadratic moment matrices have rank3 and their intended affine traction ranges remain within50–150 MPa.\n\nAll three original gauge corner locations are present; the six proposed scalar rigid-mode constraints have rank6. This phase only checks geometry and integration feasibility. No nodal force or displacement constraint was applied, no input deck or native job was submitted and no force/moment equilibrium was claimed. Native import, shape warnings and all stress/T2 checks remain for a separately authorized phase.'),
 'SCIENTIFIC_LIMITATIONS.md':('Limits of the mesh qualification','The result is pre-solver mesh qualification. It is not native ANSYS import acceptance, equilibrium, stress tensor accuracy, T2 convergence or a qualified V1 learning label. ANSYS and AI run counts are zero. Only C02 was analysed. Historical G08/X10 work was not resumed.\n\nWhole-mesh Jacobian positivity is sampled at the frozen73 points. Expanded local checks and exact rational local Bernstein bounds strengthen the evidence, but do not certify continuous positivity of the entire mesh. SICN is also a sampled metric. Gmsh parameter metadata warnings are preserved; the exact labelled mesh round trip does not certify future CAD reparameterization.\n\nThe frozen CAD and source retain prior registration, physical-axis, actual rear/thickness and notch-radius limitations. No physical stress, residual stress, plasticity, fatigue life or independent AI generalization claim follows. The official Gmsh method documentation describes the sampled SICN API; the version-pinned primary implementation is retained under01_frozen_protocol/reference_code.'),
 'README_REPRODUCIBILITY.md':('Reproducibility and review','The original invalid M1, source arrays and qualified STEP are copied under00_integrity and01_frozen_protocol with original hashes. New M1 and M2 NPZ files contain actual nodes, Tet10 connectivity, surface Tri6 connectivity, tags and quality. Each folder also contains raw and explicitly labelled MSH exports, fidelity arrays and pass receipts. Different serializations of the same coordinates/connectivity are one candidate, not additional mesh trials.\n\nThe local repair preregistration and trial/candidate ledgers are immutable release evidence. Use the existing Phase5E Python runtime with-B. New code lives only in this R1 directory. Source routines deny historical writes and external process launches, including native solvers. Review the release with the independent standard-library verifier --dry-run; do not rerun generators inside a sealed release.\n\nExact Fraction Bernstein coefficients, independent scalar Jacobians and an independent SICN formula are inspectable. Main methods: [Gmsh4.15.2 API](https://gmsh.info/doc/texinfo/gmsh.html) and [version-pinned condition-number implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gmsh-project/gmsh/gmsh_4_15_2/src/numeric/CondNumBasis.cpp). A supplementary GradientBasis.cpp download returned404; it was not required or used. The required condition-number source and numerical cross-checks are present.')}
 for name,(title,body) in docs.items():doc(name,title,body)
 doc('FINAL_R8E10R1_DECISION.md','Final mesh-recovery decision','**R8E10R1_MESH_RECOVERY_COMPLETE**\n\n'+'\n\n'.join('**'+k+'**: `'+v+'`' for k,v in decision.items())+'\n\nOne S1 trial moved one of four eligible interior midsides; original corners, connectivity, measured surface, all external M1 nodes and the STEP stayed unchanged. One complete M1 and one complete M2 candidate passed all frozen pre-solver gates. The achieved hierarchy and BVP mesh compatibility pass.\n\nThe pair is conditionally ready for a separately authorized native C02 campaign. Native import/shape checks may still reject it. No ANSYS jobs, stresses, T2 targets or AI runs were produced here.')
